hi I'm Evan Carmichael and welcome to  another edition of modeling the masters  today we're going to look at how a girl  grew up with no money lives with her  eight siblings in a small apartment and  she would go on to be the only woman  named to Time Magazine's most  influential business people of the  century this is a story of Estee Lauder  and a top three lessons that you can  learn from her success Estee Lauder was  born in Queens New York the daughter of  Gary and Jewish immigrants most of her  childhood was spent helping her parents  make ends meet by working at the  family's hardware store as she grew up  she met Joseph Lauder a textile salesman  who she married and moved to Manhattan  with after the birth of her first child  Lauder didn't want to give up her  professional career and experimented  different ingredients to create a  skincare cream for women  she began out of her kitchen and after a  year of hard work got her big break Saks  Fifth Avenue agreed to carry her product  and it sold out within two days of it  being put on the shelves after 50-plus  year to the top of her game Estee Lauder  became the only woman on Time magazine's  list of the 20 most influential business  geniuses of the century in 2009 at state  ladder companies had over 7 billion  dollars in revenue almost 30 thousand  employees and it all began at a crowded  kitchen table  by starting from her kitchen table and  by never giving up estee lauder was able  to become the most influential business  genius of the 20th century to help you  overcome your obstacles and grow your  business  here are three action items that you can  learn from estée lauder action um number  one don't stop at the first note being  an entrepreneur means you're going to  get a lot of rejection whether it's  friends and family telling you that your  idea will never be successful or  prospects and customers telling you they  don't want to buy from you you'll get a  lot of notes successful entrepreneurs  pick themselves back up after rejection  and keep improving their products and  messaging until they get to a yes Lauda  was known for her unwavering persistence  when she was trying to expand her  European market she arranged a meeting  with a manager of galleries lafayette  Europe's largest department store when a  manager said no she accidentally spilled  her perfume samples on the floor and the  store customers started asking how they  could buy some of the fragrance the  manager had to give her a contract  according to Lauder I have never worked  a day in my life without selling if I  believe in something I sell it and I  sell it hard if you have a goal if you  want to be successful if you really want  to do it and become another estee lauder  you've got to work hard you've got to  stick to it and you've got to believe in  what you're doing  Akshat item number to love what you do  any successful entrepreneur will tell  you that one of the keys to their  success is that they love what they do  when you really love your business you  not only enjoy it more but you put the  kind of time and energy and that's  needed for a company to take off you see  what the details constantly improve your  offering not just because it'll make you  money but because you love doing it  lahter loved her product so much that  she paid attention to every little  detail when she got her first deal with  saxis Avenue she stood at the entrance  door for an entire week and watched the  women come in nine times out of ten the  first place her eyes would wander would  be to the right not to the left not  straight ahead so she asked for her  product we placed on the right  according to Lauder I love my product I  love to touch the creams smell them look  at them carry them with me a person has  to love her harvest if she is to expect  others to love it  action item number three sell sell sell  not all entrepreneurs and natural  salespeople but you have to learn how to  sell if you want to build a business of  any significant size more entrepreneurs  fail because they can't sell rather than  them not having a good product or  service  when Lada was first getting started she  didn't have money to spend on  advertising and promotions so she  invested her time into product demos she  began at salons hotels subway stations  and even people on the street offering  them a free makeover and the chance to  buy her products she eventually moved  the sell to the big department stores  but it all began on a $0 budget and her  grinding out sale after sale  according to Lauder if you put the  product into the customers hands it will  speak for itself if it's something of  quality if you don't sell it's not the  product that's wrong it's you  so remember don't stop at the first note  love what you do and sell sell sell to  finish this video I wanted to share one  my favorite true stories about Estee  Lauder and some of her top quotes one  slaughter built up enough money to start  a marketing campaign  she went to various advertising agencies  all turned her down because a company  was too small with only $50,000 as  friend she used her entire budget on  samples that she would send out as  direct mail campaigns and free gifts  with purchases it proved to be a  successful move and she changed the way  beauty products were marketed  thank you for joining me for another  edition of modeling the masters if you  enjoyed please give the video a thumbs  up I'd also love to hear your thoughts  if you want to leave a comment below and  stay tuned for the next episode
 

